Shri Prahlad said,
To our forefathers, the Mandara mountain is situated in penance. The gods, with their intellect, undertook the war against the demons. 2. Meaning of the word.

Shri-Prahlad said—Prahlad Maharaj said; Pitari—Asura father Hiranyakashipu's; Prasthite—Upon leaving from here; Asmakam—Our; Tapase—To do penance; Mandara-achalam—On the mountain named Mandarachal; Yuddha-udyamam—The effort to wage war; Param—Great; Chakrur—Established; Vibudha—Indra and other gods; Danavan—Of the Asuras; Prati—To. Prahlada Maharaj said: When our father Hiranyakashipu went to Mandarachal mountain to perform rigorous penance,
in his absence, Indra and other gods made a fierce attempt to suppress all the demons in the war. Pipilikarahivrishtiya lokopatapanah.
Papan papoobhakshiti vadanto vasavadayah. 3. Meaning of the word

Pipilikaiha - by small ants; Ahih - snake; Iva - like; Dishtya - Oh; Lok-upatapanah - always of all;
Oppressor; Papan - from one's own sinful deeds; Papah - sinful; Abhakshi - eaten; Iti - thus;
Vadantah - while saying; Vasava-Aadih - King Indra and other gods. "Ouch! Just as small ants eat a snake, similarly, the tormenting
Hiranyakashipu, who brought destruction upon all kinds of people due to his own sins,
has been defeated." Saying this, Indradi Devatas made a plan to fight the Asuras.
Made. Teshamatibalodyam nishamyasurayuthapaah. The gods were struck, and all directions trembled. 4>. Kalatrupratyaksha, by the touch of an animal.
Those who are not noticed, all those who are in distress. 5. Meaning of the word:

Tesham—of the gods, Indra, etc.; Atibala—excessive strength and effort; Nishamya—by listening; Asur-yutpah—the mighty leaders of the demons; Vadhyamanaah—being killed one after another; Suraih—by the gods; Bhitah—frightened; Dudruvuhu—gone;
Sarvatham—in all; Disham—in directions; Kalatra—wives; Putra-vitt—sons and property; Aptan—related; Grihan—in houses;
Pashu-parichhadan—animals and household items; Na—not; Avekshyamanaah—seeing; Tvaritaah—quickly;
Sarve—all; Prana-paripisvah—excessively desiring to live;
